  "english": "24. Thursday. Tone 6 [Gk - Gadz]. Prophet David and James the Apostle.\n\n27. Sunday. Tone 1 [Adz]. Sixth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [Gk]: \"Who is from eternity\" (Nakhahavitean). Morning Office [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [Adz]: \"Awe-inspiring\" (Soskali), to the end.\n\n29. Tuesday. Tone 2 [BdZ]. James and John. Barekendan of the Fast of the Nativity.\n\n30. Wednesday. Tone 3 [Bk]. Fast of the Nativity. Canticle [Harts] Tone 8 [Dk]: \"Blessed are you, Lord God of our fathers, and blessed is your name.\"\n\nJanuary.\n\n2. Saturday. Tone 4 [Dz]. The Holy Hierarchs Basil of Caesarea, and the others.\n\n3. Sunday. Tone 5 [Dk]. Seventh [Sunday], of the Fast. Morning Office [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [Dk]: \"Glory to the resurrection,\" to the end.\n\n4. Monday. Tone 1 [Adz]. Fast. Canticle of Penitence [Harts ahts] Tone 1 [Adz]: \"The children sang.\"\n\n5. Tuesday. Tone 2 [Ak]. Eve of the Nativity and Theophany of Christ our God.\nEnd of the year.\n\nThe Seven-Day Week of the Romans.\nJanuary.\n\n6. MONDAY. Tone 2 [BdZ]. Feast of the Nativity and Theophany of Christ our God. The dispensation of eating [non-fasting period] is seven days.\n\n12. Sunday. Tone 1 [Adz]. Barekendan of the Fast of the Catechumens. - 7th day of the Nativity of Christ.\n\n13. Monday. Tone 2 [Ak]. Fast of the Catechumens. - Feast of the Nativity and the Octave of the Circumcision of Christ.\n\n14. Tuesday. Tone 4 [Dz]. Fast. Canticle of Penitence [Harts ahts] Tone 2 [Ak]: \"Glorified.\"\n\n18. Saturday. Tone 4 [Dz]. Saint John the Forerunner.\n\n19. Sunday. Tone 5 [Dk]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [Dz]: \"Glorifying.\" Morning Office [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [Dk]: \"Glory to the resurrection.\"\n\n20. Monday. Tone 1 [Adz]. Saint Sargis and his son Mardiros, and the fourteen soldiers, and the Atomian generals.\n\n26. Sunday. Tone 4 [Dz]. Mid-Lent [Mijink]. Morning Office [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [Gz]: \"The Resurrection.\" See the First Volume up to Transfiguration [Vardavar], keeping the order of this place.\n\nFebruary.\n\n2. Sunday. Tone 5 [Dk]. Real Barekendan [of Great Lent].\n\n14. Friday. Tone 3 [Bk]. Fast. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj].\n\nMarch.\n\n23. Sunday. Tone 1 [Adz]. Easter [Zatik]: Day of the Resurrection of Christ our God. For the others, see the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n\nApril.\n\n7. Monday. Tone 5 [Dk]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin Mary.\n\nMay.\n\n1. Thursday. Tone 6 [Gk]. Day of the Ascension of Christ God.\n\n11. Sunday. Tone 2 [Ak]. Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Barekendan of the Fast of Elijah.\n\n18. Sunday. Tone 1 [Adz]. First [Sunday]. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Canticle [Harts] Tone 1 [Adz]: \"Who came for the salvation of the universe.\"",
